      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not very sure but I think there *might* be a bug here in the following scenario.\n\n• Network connects, IPv6 comes up\n• update() → Prefix discovery starts\n• Prefix is discovered\n• update() → start()\n• go to running state and hum happily\n• IPv4 shows up\n• update() → stop() → IDLE\n• IPv4 disappears\n• update() → startPrefixDiscovery()\nHere the old code would go directly to started, and the new code will go to DISCOVERING. The new code flow is cleaner but I don\u0027t think anybody is going to call update() again until something else happens.\n\nThis is because AFAICT we don\u0027t clear the prefix when v4 shows up (though I haven\u0027t looked at whether netd does call back up to clear) ; if we do, then this can\u0027t happen. It\u0027s also fairly unlikely a network will lose v4 but keep v6 connectivity I guess.",
